# Underworld Breach's escape is judged and costed on the half being cast (CR 709.3): Life // Death escapes as Death for Death's {1}{B}
# plus three exiled cards, not for the two halves' {G} + {1}{B}, and not for Life's {G}, which no mana here could pay. Bot1's Mox Jet and Mox
# Pearl pay {1}{B}; Death returns the Marauding Mako (mana value 1) to the battlefield and Bot1 loses 1 life. The Lotus pays for Breach and
# Faithless Looting, which discards Life // Death and the Mako; Lightning Bolt (Mox Ruby) is the third card exiled besides the Lotus and
# the Looting; the sorcery, resolved, goes back to the graveyard. Breach is sacrificed at the end step, so it all happens on turn 3.

